f it's not set up for  that to me it's just it's so much better  when I can really focus on making sure  that the you know I'm focusing and kind  of manipulating my body's positioning to  make sure it's just perfect application  of that force for the each individual  quad and another thing I like to do Greg  you and I've talked about this for  whatever reason we both grew up near  gyms that had the just this beautiful  hammer strength horizontal leg press  with a slightly tilted foot platform and  that machine is wild and I do that and  unilateral fashion as well and I'm  actually pretty upset because I used to  love that machine I no longer have  access to it and it was just my favorite  thing in the world and then finally you  can't have this discussion without  talking about the the traditional hack  squat machine with the load positioned  over the shoulders I don't I don't like  the the kind of newer generation that  they're called hack squats but it's it's  like you're the load is more situated  near the hips yeah I it like puts you  into like some pretty serious lumbar  flexion as like a starting point I'm not  a big fan of that I like the traditional  you know at an angle weight on the  shoulders hack squat I I agree with all  of those for the most part so if the the  way this question was asked is what are  the best exercises for increasing quad  size specifically for the squat and so  the way I'm looking at this is like if  you're if if you don't have another  muscle group that's limiting you just  squat like do some form of squat you're  not going to be able to train your quads  specifically for the squat better than  you can with the squat and so then when  I start thinking about accessory  exercises I'm approaching it with with  that context in mind that basically this  person needs more quad work than they  can get from the squat which could be  for for a couple different reasons one  maybe someone has some sort of back  issue or some sort of hip issue 